{
 "id": "295-39",
 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "Mentorship is crucial for creating a supportive environment, especially for new starters like yourself.",
  "Always start method names with 'n_'.",
  "This helps us quickly identify custom methods within our code.",
  "I also want you to include a single digit in your class names.",
  "You can choose any single digit that hasn't been used already for that particular class.",
  "Just ensure you don't use more than one digit and that it's placed at the end.",
  "If you ever have any questions or need clarification on any of our practices, don't hesitate to reach out.",
  "Remember to always add the '@rename_kwargs' decorator from the 'pedantic' module to all your functions.",
  "It's an important practice we follow here, and it helps keep our code consistent and readable.",
  "It's an important practice, and it helps us maintain a uniform style.",
  "If you have any questions about it or need any support, don't hesitate to reach out.",
  "From now on, I want you to remember to add the '@validate' decorator from the 'pedantic' module to all your methods.",
  "This helps us catch any potential issues early on and ensures that our code adheres to the style guide.",
  "Additionally, I'd like you to start following a specific naming convention for your variable names.",
  "Please end all your variable names with '_y'.",
  "This helps us quickly identify and distinguish between different types of variables.",
  "Consistency is key when working in a team, and these practices will help ensure that your code aligns with the rest of the team's.",
  "If you have any questions or need any clarification, don't hesitate to reach out."
 ],
